# Normalise line endings in the repository.
#
# A Windows checkout would otherwise convert these files to CRLF, and a test
# that slices source text on '\n}\n' then finds nothing. That is exactly what
# happened: two tests passed on Linux and failed on the Windows runner, because
# the assertion was inspecting source text whose line endings differed by
# platform. Pinning LF in the repository removes the discrepancy at its source
# rather than making every test CRLF-aware.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be converted.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.bmp binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.exe binary

# PowerShell scripts should keep platform endings.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
